WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.675
FISMA is a staffing requirement
as much as a course requirement.

2
00:00:03.675 --> 00:00:07.281
The agency head must have enough
trained people to comply,

3
00:00:07.281 --> 00:00:11.788
and the CIO trains and oversees those
with significant security duties.

4
00:00:11.788 --> 00:00:16.640
OPM's rule names five audiences, from
every user to IT operations staff,

5
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.325
and agencies must code their cyber
positions to the NICE Framework,

6
00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:23.500
NIST's vocabulary of work roles.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.663
But those codes haven't been reliable.

8
00:00:25.663 --> 00:00:31.130
GAO found most agencies had miscoded a
share of their IT management positions,

9
00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.588
so the program treats codes as one
roster input, not settled fact.

10
00:00:35.588 --> 00:00:38.462
Just as important is what
the rules don't require.

11
00:00:38.462 --> 00:00:41.861
There's no civilian certification
mandate, and the Defense

12
00:00:41.861 --> 00:00:46.024
Department's certification program
doesn't apply to civilian agencies.

13
00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:48.550
Now, what the program actually teaches.
